- Upon completing A, move on to task B as it is now executable due to the fulfillment of its only remaining criterion: having been preceded by 'A'; 
- Finally, after finishing with B which had a dependency solely tied up from completion of ‘A’ and has no further dependencies itself—only for C's execution does this task have any prerequisites (that is being completed just recently). Hence completing the last operation.  
